      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When looking to source parts from Vietnam, you can generally expect a reliable vendor base, with many established suppliers following international quality standards. Vietnam has a well-developed manufacturing industry, and suppliers often have good logistics and communication skills. However, some Vietnamese vendors may require lengthy negotiations, particularly for complex or high-value components.\n\nIn contrast, Nigeria has faced challenges with vendor reliability, with many suppliers struggling to provide consistent and high-quality components, particularly in the electronics industry. Business culture in Nigeria is often characterized as collectivist, where building relationships and trust takes precedence over strict adherence to timelines and protocols. This can lead to longer lead times and more negotiations during the procurement process.",
